    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 permeability records show that zwitterionic acids and piperidine-aryl drugs can have measurable intestinal permeability: fexofenadine human Peff 2.61×10^-5 cm/s and rat Peff 7.04×10^-6 cm/s, haloperidol Caco-2 Papp 14.5×10^-6 cm/s, and loperamide fraction absorbed 65–100%.",
