      "claim": "L5 gut-wall records are mechanistically mixed: fexofenadine is a P-gp substrate with pure-drug efflux ratio 2.69 and P-gp inhibition raises exposure, but grepafloxacin A→B 2.60×10^-5 cm/s, ramatroban near-complete absorption, and asimadoline absorption ≥20% in 1 h independent of P-gp show that efflux is not threshold-determinative; no L5 record provides a direct low-F outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C184","C188","C173","C170","C178","C177"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic metabolism records do not establish sub-20% F: haloperidol is extensively metabolized by CYP3A4/UGT (HLM CLint 38 µL/min/mg for O-glucuronidation; CYP3A4 oxidation) yet has F 35±8%; meperidine is N-demethylated by multiple P450s yet has F ~48–80%; cilomilast, the closest cyclohexane-nitrile/acid analog, is only shown to undergo CYP2C8 3-hydroxylation; mitraphylline's rapid HLM metabolism has no linked F outcome.",
      "card_ids": ["C245","C251","C221","C225","C203","C217","C231","C236","C238","C234","C246","C252","C227","C232","C213","C244","C204"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only sub-20% F record, ampicillin in fasted veal calves at 12%, is species-specific and not transferable to a human-oriented query prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C31"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C245","C251","C227","C232","C213","C244","C204"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query; prediction remains transfer-based.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability measurement is available; L6 records are analog-based with low transfer likelihood.",
